{
  "comment": [
    "Cross-language golden vectors for the canonical Decimal wire encoding:",
    "the signed unscaled integer (value * 10^scale) as exactly 8 bytes,",
    "little-endian, two's complement. See the BytesArray comment in",
    "milvus-proto schema.proto for the contract.",
    "",
    "Every implementation (Go, C++, and each SDK) must map literal -> unscaled",
    "-> bytes_le_hex identically. An identical copy of this file lives at",
    "internal/core/unittest/testdata/decimal/golden_vectors.json for the C++",
    "side; keep the two in sync."
  ],
  "cases": [
